{
 "summary": "Checkout failures originate in orders: orders logs 'database connection refused' (62 times from 00:38:42Z) on the same traces where gateway logs 'orders returned 500', and gateway returns 502. The failing requests fail fast (3-31ms), which points to a refused database connection rather than a timeout cascade. The database itself is not covered by the evidence, and no deployment records were found in the window.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "The orders service (release 2.7.0) cannot connect to its database ('database connection refused'). It returns 500 on POST /orders, and gateway surfaces this as 502 on POST /checkout.",
  "service": "orders",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-7cd2f3a75ebc",
   "ev-208428dea34d",
   "ev-81c0b161784a",
   "ev-7a43f4491f3b"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway passes orders 500s through as 502s, so the gateway 5xx ratio (avg 9.7%, max 28.0%) rises just after the orders 5xx ratio (avg 14.9%, max 36.9%).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-315784d5813e",
    "ev-7a43f4491f3b",
    "ev-81c0b161784a"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "p95 latency rose to about 0.9s on both gateway and orders, with no latency onset flagged. The sampled error traces are fast (3-31ms), so the slowness is on other requests and is not explained by the evidence.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-315784d5813e",
    "ev-7a43f4491f3b",
    "ev-81c0b161784a"
   ]
  }
 ],
